OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking, out of scope for U7F — attributed by
`git diff HEAD` / `git show HEAD:...`, both PRE-EXISTING in HEAD da2fbca,
untouched by this uncommitted diff):

- OBS-1 (same defect class, different mechanism, insights page only):
  `web/templates/pages/insights.html:22` passes
  `"InputHxAttrs" (safeHTML "hx-get=... hx-target=... hx-trigger=change ...")`
  into `shared/range-picker.html` lines 96/103
  (`{{if .InputHxAttrs}}{{.InputHxAttrs}}{{end}}`, mid-tag, not inside a
  quoted attribute value). `safeHTML` returns `template.HTML` (render.go:749),
  not `template.HTMLAttr`; html/template's contextual escaper can't safely
  splice `template.HTML` into a bare-attribute-list position and substitutes
  `ZgotmplZ` for the whole blob — confirmed live: both the From and To date
  inputs on /insights render literally `ZgotmplZ` where `hx-get`,
  `hx-target`, `hx-select`, `hx-include`, `hx-push-url`, `hx-trigger`,
  `hx-indicator` should be. This means typing/changing the date inputs
  directly on /insights does NOT trigger an HTMX refresh at all (the preset
  buttons still work per finding 2 above — this only affects the manual
  date-input path). Present in HEAD (da2fbca) before this uncommitted
  diff — confirmed via `git show HEAD:web/templates/components/shared/
  range-picker.html` (identical lines) and `git diff HEAD -- range-picker.html`
  (U7F's diff doesn't touch lines 90-105). Recommend a same-defect-class
  follow-up task: change `InputHxAttrs`'s type to `template.HTMLAttr` (or
  restructure to individual `{{if}}` per hx-attribute, as the fixed preset
  buttons now do) and add a render-test asserting the hx-* attributes are
  real and ZgotmplZ is absent on /insights, mirroring this test's pattern.
- OBS-2: dashboard/insights presets use non-numeric string values
  (ytd/1m/2m/.../all) vs explorer/major-expenses numeric strings
  (0/1/2/3/6/12) — both work correctly with the fix since it branches on
  attribute NAME not value; noted only for completeness, not a defect.

No FAILs against ACCESSIBILITY.md or WCAG 2.2 AA within U7F's scope.
